**Manufacturing Procedures:**  
All assembly operations within the Manufacturing Unit must adhere to ISO 9001 standards to ensure product quality. Daily audits will be conducted by the Safety Officer (Emily Johnson) in collaboration with Production Manager David Smith. Any deviations must be reported to the Quality Assurance Team (QAT) led by Sarah Brown.

**Safety Compliance:**  
The Manufacturing Unit operates under Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) guidelines. All employees must complete safety training conducted quarterly by Safety Specialist Mike Thompson. Personal Protective Equipment (PPE) must be worn at all times within the facility, and compliance will be monitored through monthly inspections.

**Packaging Rules:**  
The Packaging Department must utilize eco-friendly materials sourced from GreenPack Solutions. Packaging designs must be approved by the Marketing Team, overseen by Laura White. All products should be labeled with the production date and batch number, as per the standard established on December 10, 2023.

**Distribution Procedures:**  
The Distribution Center follows a Just-In-Time (JIT) inventory system to optimize shipping efficiency. All outgoing shipments must be logged into the ERP system (SAP) by Logistics Coordinator James Wilson. Delivery routes are to be planned by the Transport Team, under the supervision of Operations Manager Rachel Green. Regular feedback from the customer service department, led by Tom Harris, must be integrated into distribution planning to enhance service quality.

